  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Running** (1 other source): Running flows directly into Running The Route in the first set, marked as a segue [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Foundations Of Stone**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **This Old World Home**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **From The Forrest**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **In My Tree**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **Down In The Swamp**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **You Must Come In At The Door**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [5]\n- **Feast Here Tonight**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- **I Peed On A Bird**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Nights In White Satin [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2022-10-30.sibert.matrix.flac16** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 27 songs; 166 min [1]\n- **billystrings2022-10-30**: source not stated; 27 songs; 164 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]\n- **billystrings2022-10-30.DPA4018**: source not stated; 27 songs; 163 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Notes list the band as William Apostle, Royal Masat, Jarrod Walker, Billy Failing, Rushad Eggleston and Ahn Phung, including cello and flute [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2022-10-30.sibert.matrix.flac16**: taped by Ryan Sibert; source: Studio Project C4 {cardioid/DIN} + Church CA-14 {omni/mono} > Ugly Box >> Tascam DR-70 > wav (24/48) [1]. Also: Transfer path went from SD card to PC, then Reaper, CDWavEditor, TLH and foobar2000, ending as 16-bit FLAC [1]\n- **billystrings2022-10-30**: taped by Z-Man; transferred by Z-Man; source: Schoeps CCM4V'S>Lunatec V2>Sound Devices 722 (24/44.1) [2]. Also: Processed from the 722 through Sound Forge 10 and CD Wave to 16-bit FLAC, tagged in Foobar2000; seeded by Z-Man [2]\n- **billystrings2022-10-30.DPA4018**: taped by John Bell; transferred by John Bell; source: DPA 4018GR (DINa)> DPA MMA 6000> Sony PCM-A10 @24/48 [3]",
